			"Message": "fix(Worker): Prevent Service Worker refresh loop with version tracking\n\nThis commit resolves a critical bug where the Service Worker would trigger infinite page reloads. The `activate` event handler now tracks `CurrentClientVersion` and only notifies clients when a genuine version change is detected, preventing redundant `postMessage` calls that caused the refresh loop.\n\nThe registration logic in `Register.ts` has been restructured to remove the `controllerchange` and `message` event listeners that contributed to the loop. A new `CheckForUpdate` function provides explicit update checking, and the control flow now properly manages the `WorkerRegistered` session state.\n\nSecondary changes include:\n- Documentation overhaul with system architecture diagram (Mermaid), component breakdown, and improved formatting\n- ESBuild configuration updated to silence `suspicious-logical-operator` warnings\n- TypeScript configuration simplified by removing `composite` and `declarationMap` options",
			"SHA": "ddd814b6fd5c09bd81e7c56f7d6c0a673320ddab"
		},
